&lt;div class=&quot;content-intro&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Company Overview:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Beam Therapeutics is a biotechnology company committed to establishing the leading, fully integrated platform for precision genetic medicines. To achieve this vision, Beam has assembled a platform with integrated gene editing, delivery and internal manufacturing capabilities. Beam’s suite of gene editing technologies is anchored by base editing, a proprietary technology that is designed to enable precise, predictable and efficient single base changes, at targeted genomic sequences, without making double-stranded breaks in the DNA. This has the potential to enable a wide range of therapeutic editing strategies that Beam is using to advance a diversified portfolio of base editing programs. Beam is a values-driven organization committed to its people, cutting-edge science, and a vision of providing life-long cures to patients suffering from serious diseases.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Position Overview:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Beam Therapeutics is seeking a highly skilled attorney to serve as the Corporate Counsel/Senior Corporate Counsel, Commercial Contracts. This role will partner with Beam’s medical affairs, commercial and manufacturing teams to provide contracting support for Beam’s transition to a commercial stage company. Ideal candidates will excel in negotiating complex agreements, managing risk, and achieving business objectives in a fast-paced, cutting-edge biotechnology company.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Responsibilities:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Draft and negotiate high-stakes agreements in support of Beam’s anticipated product launches, including complex commercial contracts with gene therapy treatment centers, channel partners and manufacturers.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Assist with legal review of other pre-commercial activities, including advisory boards, patient engagement events, patient support programs, market access activities, speaker programs, and market research.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Provide legal support to Beam’s various promotional material review committees.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Provide ongoing contracting support and lifecycle management, including agreement interpretation and risk analysis, for Beam’s commercial, medical affairs, manufacturing and other teams.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Collaborate with business teams and subject matter experts on continuous review and updates of Beam contracting playbooks and standards.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Draft and negotiate a range of other key agreements in support of Beam’s broader business, including licensing agreements, collaborations, clinical trial agreements, and sponsored research agreements.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Qualifications:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;JD from an accredited law school; admission to practice in at least one U.S. jurisdiction.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;5+ years of experience with complex biotechnology contracting, ideally with commercial-stage cell and gene therapy companies.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ability to manage multiple, overlapping, high-stakes agreements to completion on tight timelines.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Flexible, must be able to work collaboratively with team members for a diverse range of projects.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;High degree of professional ethics and integrity.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Sound judgement and ability to quickly analyze different sources of information.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Practical and business-minded, capable of recognizing, assessing, and responding to urgent matters with timely, pragmatic, and clear solutions.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Exceptional and demonstrated written and verbal communication skills.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Candidates are expected to come onsite 2 days per week&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Additive Qualifications:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience advising medical affairs and commercial teams on legal and regulatory legal requirements related to product launches.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ability to provide legal counsel on health care laws, such as anti-kickback, false claims and transparency statutes.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Service on promotional material review committees for pre-commercial or commercial biotechnology companies.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;content-pay-transparency&quot;&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;pay-input&quot;&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;description&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;The salary range below reflects the full-time base salary range we expect to pay for this role at the time of posting. Base pay will be determined based on several factors including, but not limited to, relevant experience, education, scope of job, internal comparisons, and market data.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;title&quot;&gt;Beam Pay Range&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;pay-range&quot;&gt;&lt;span&gt;$210,000&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class=&quot;divider&quot;&gt;&amp;mdash;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span&gt;$320,000 USD&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;

&lt;div class=&quot;content-intro&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Company Overview:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Beam Therapeutics is a biotechnology company committed to establishing the leading, fully integrated platform for precision genetic medicines. To achieve this vision, Beam has assembled a platform with integrated gene editing, delivery and internal manufacturing capabilities. Beam’s suite of gene editing technologies is anchored by base editing, a proprietary technology that is designed to enable precise, predictable and efficient single base changes, at targeted genomic sequences, without making double-stranded breaks in the DNA. This has the potential to enable a wide range of therapeutic editing strategies that Beam is using to advance a diversified portfolio of base editing programs. Beam is a values-driven organization committed to its people, cutting-edge science, and a vision of providing life-long cures to patients suffering from serious diseases.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Position Overview:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p class=&quot;isSelectedEnd&quot;&gt;The Director, Field Market Access will serve as the primary field market access leader within a defined geographic region. This role is responsible for engaging and negotiating with payers, partnering with Treatment Centers on billing and coding, and collaborating with key stakeholders to support patient access across the Beam portfolio.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;This field-based position will execute market access strategies focused on payer engagement, reimbursement, contracting, affordability, and patient access. As a key member of the commercial organization, this individual will play a critical role in supporting coverage and ensuring appropriate patient access for Beam&#39;s first commercial product, risto-cel, an investigational ex vivo gene therapy being studied for the treatment of Sickle Cell Disease.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;We are actively hiring for several positions across regions nationwide.&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Responsibilities:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Negotiate directly with Commercial and Government Payers to ensure pricing and coverage for the Beam portfolio, potentially including managed Medicaid and Medicaid FFS.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Execute the Market Access&amp;nbsp;Strategies for the Beam portfolio with Payers and Treatment Centers, including communicating economic value propositions.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Educate providers on local payer trends, appropriate billing and coding for gene therapy, providing support to offices for individual patient reimbursement journeys, including troubleshooting reimbursement concerns.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Monitor, analyze, and influence local payer trends in rare disease and gene therapy to ensure environment supports innovation&amp;nbsp;in gene therapy affordability and accessibility.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Provide training and education programs on reimbursement best practices and health policy issues to internal stakeholders and external stakeholders, such as Treatment Centers.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Work seamlessly with cross&amp;nbsp;functional field pod (Medical Affairs, Gene Therapy Operations,&amp;nbsp;Key Account Management) to support&amp;nbsp;access and coverage of Beam’s&amp;nbsp;portfolio.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Develop&amp;nbsp;local / regional&amp;nbsp;relationships with professional societies, medical associations, advocacy groups, thought leaders and trade groups for the purposes of driving comprehensive coverage and adequate payment.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Qualifications:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Bachelor&#39;s degree required; advanced degree preferred.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;10+ years of progressive experience in the pharmaceutical or biotech industry with 5+ years in market access, including field roles.&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Hospital and payer experience establishing coverage policies&amp;nbsp;for complex therapies required.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Demonstrated success in building and managing relationships with payers and financial decision-makers in Treatment Centers.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Must have established relationships with payers (Commercial payers – required; Medicaid – preferred). &amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Buy &amp;amp; bill experience required; Experience in cell or gene therapy preferred.&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience working in local, cross-functional field teams, including&amp;nbsp;Key&amp;nbsp;Account&amp;nbsp;Managers, MSLs, and Patient Operations.&amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Excellent communication, presentation, and negotiation skills.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Proficiency with CRM systems, PowerPoint, and Excel.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Willingness to travel approximately 50% of the time/as needed.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;em&gt;Beam’s field team operates through an account-based pod model (a team structure that groups cross-functional specialists together to manage a specific segment of accounts from lead to close). The Director, Key Account Manager (KAM), owns the integrated account strategy, account plan, and overall account performance. The Director, Field Market Access owns access, reimbursement and payer engagement. The Associate Director/Director, Gene Therapy Operations (GTO) owns site operational readiness and apheresis and patient logistics executions. Each role and team is expected to work cross functionally while maintaining clear functional accountability.&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;content-pay-transparency&quot;&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;pay-input&quot;&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;description&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;The salary range below reflects the full-time base salary range we expect to pay for this role at the time of posting. Base pay will be determined based on several factors including, but not limited to, relevant experience, education, scope of job, internal comparisons, and market data.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;title&quot;&gt;Beam Pay Range&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;pay-range&quot;&gt;&lt;span&gt;$210,000&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class=&quot;divider&quot;&gt;&amp;mdash;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span&gt;$260,000 USD&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;

